+## 📌 CVE-2022-33064 – False Positive in libsndfile
+
+- **Component:** libsndfile
+- **Issue:** Reported off-by-one error in `wav_read_header` in `src/wav.c`
+- **Impact:** Claimed out-of-bounds write / denial of service / possible code execution via crafted WAV input
+- **Debian Status:** ✅ **Non-issue / false positive**
+  → [Debian Security Tracker – CVE-2022-33064](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2022-33064)
+  → [Debian Bug #1051890](https://bugs.debian.org/cgi-bin/bugreport.cgi?bug=1051890)
+
+### Vulnerable Versions (Debian)
+| Release | Package    | Status                   |
+|---------|------------|--------------------------|
+| Debian  | libsndfile | Not affected / Non-issue |
+
+---
+
+### Why You Can't Fix This
+
+- ✅ Debian’s security tracker explicitly marks **CVE-2022-33064** as a **non-issue in libsndfile**
+- ✅ The Debian tracker notes that **upstream disputes this as a possible false positive**
+- ✅ Debian does **not** treat this as a confirmed vulnerability requiring a package fix
+- ✅ There is therefore **no Debian patch to carry** for this CVE
+- ✅ Scanner hits are most likely caused by **CVE database matching**, not a real affected Debian package state
+
+**✅ Recommendation:**
+Document this CVE as a **false positive / non-issue for Debian**. No remediation patch is required.
